INT. ABANDONED DRIVE-IN PROJECTION BOOTH - NIGHT

A cinderblock room, the size of a closet. A dead projector the color of old teeth squats in the middle. Spray-painted names cover the walls. A battery lantern throws everything into hard shadow.

YUSUF HAMDAN (17, thin, nervous laugh, a cheap digital camera on a strap) sits on an overturned crate. Beside him, LUCINDA "LUCKY" MORROW (17, bleached hair, scraped knees) plays with a lighter. BARNABY QUILL (18, built like a linebacker, soft voice) blocks the doorway. DAHLIA REYES (16, hoodie, headphones around her neck) holds a flask she shouldn't have. MAGNUS WICK (17, varsity jacket, too clean) stands apart from them.

LUCKY
You said you'd be here at nine.

MAGNUS
I was here at nine.

DAHLIA
You were not here at nine, I was here at nine, I sat alone for twenty minutes--

YUSUF
It's not a big deal, we're all here now--

LUCKY
It is a big deal! We swore. After graduation, nobody leaves without--

BARNABY
Lucky.

LUCKY
--without saying it to everyone, that's the rule!

MAGNUS
There's no rule. You made it up.

DAHLIA
She did not make it up, we all signed the wall.

Dahlia jabs a finger at the concrete. Under a layer of paint, five signatures sit in a ragged circle.

YUSUF
(trying to joke)
Technically, I signed it in marker. Pretty permanent.

MAGNUS
I'm going to Dartmouth. Fine? I got in. It's done. I didn't want to tell you like this.

Silence. Then everyone speaks at once.

LUCKY
Dartmouth?

BARNABY
You said Ohio State.

DAHLIA
Why would you lie about that?

YUSUF
Congratulations, I guess?

MAGNUS
Because I knew you'd all look like this!

Barnaby steps in from the doorway. Magnus doesn't back up.

BARNABY
Like what?

MAGNUS
Like I already left.

Lucky snaps the lighter shut. The lantern flickers. Yusuf lifts the camera and, without asking, takes one picture of all of them.

The flash leaves white afterimages. Nobody says anything.
